# Copy to an ignored local .env file only when needed. Never commit real
# credentials, a Service URI, or a value copied from a production database.

# Required by `cargo run -p server --bin contracter-server`.
# Use a least-privileged runtime role in deployed environments. For every
# sensitive value set exactly one source: the direct variable OR its `_FILE`
# alternative. Production deployments should prefer read-only secret files.
DATABASE_URL=postgres://USER@HOST:PORT/contracter?sslmode=require
# DATABASE_URL_FILE=/run/secrets/database_url

# Required 32-byte keys encoded as unpadded base64url.
# QUOTE_SIGNING_KEY=REPLACE_WITH_LOCAL_ONLY_VALUE
# QUOTE_SIGNING_KEY_FILE=/run/secrets/quote_signing_key
# QUOTE_SEED_KEY=REPLACE_WITH_LOCAL_ONLY_VALUE
# QUOTE_SEED_KEY_FILE=/run/secrets/quote_seed_key

# Used only by `./scripts/verify.sh`. This must point to a disposable,
# isolated database: the integration fixtures intentionally write data.
TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgres://USER@HOST:PORT/contracter_test?sslmode=require

# Canonical skin artwork is imported server-side and served from controlled CDN/object storage.
CONTRACTER_IMAGE_BASE_URL=https://cdn.example.com/contracter
# Frontend API origin for local development.
VITE_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8080
# Optional frontend override for development catalog artwork.
VITE_SKIN_CDN_URL=https://cdn.example.com/contracter

# Optional server settings. Defaults: HOST=127.0.0.1, PORT=8080,
# LOG_FILTER=info. Do not set INSECURE_COOKIES outside local HTTP development.
# HOST=127.0.0.1
# PORT=8080
# LOG_FILTER=info
# RATE_LIMIT_BURST=30
# TRUSTED_PROXY_CIDRS=172.30.0.0/24
# INSECURE_COOKIES=true

# Internal money is CC (Contracter Coins), stored as integer micro-CC.
# RUB is accepted only by a future server-side payment webhook; never put a
# client-supplied exchange rate or fiat amount into ledger APIs.

# Optional server-side Market.CSGO evidence importer. Never expose this key to
# the frontend, commit it, or print it in logs.
# MARKET_CSGO_API_KEY=REPLACE_IN_SERVER_SECRET_STORE
# MARKET_RUB_TO_CC_RATE=1

# Prefer a hidden terminal prompt instead of writing a password to a file:
# read -s "PGPASSWORD?PostgreSQL password: "; export PGPASSWORD; echo
